{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/829416-what-are-the-iconic-dragon-blooded-charms","id":829416,"title":"What are the iconic Dragon-Blooded Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-13T14:31:50-08:00","id":829416,"title":"What are the iconic Dragon-Blooded Charms?","content":"Exactly what it says on the tin. I'm converting Exalted to a different system to run for my group, but it's a long time since I played it for any length of time and I don't really have the sense of the Charm sets any more that I used to have. So I'm asking everyone here -what Dragon-Blooded charms do you think are the most iconic and recognizable ones, the ones that are &quot;signature&quot; powers of the Terrestrials? I'm after both general and Elemental effects and the more Aspect-spesific ones.<br /> <br /> Elemental Bolt Attack, Dragon-Graced Weapon and its equivalents in the other combat abilities are what spring to mind for me as bread-and-butter combat effects, as well as the anima flux itself, even though it's not actually a Charm. There's the Immaculate Styles, in theory, but I don't really have a good picture of what each of them actually does for you in a fight, beyond Fire Dragon letting you make super-fast attacks and Water Dragon letting you control people's blood. There's Unassailable Body of Element, which isn't really a staple the way the dodge tree is built, but has the imagery of one, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> There's Oath of the Ten Thousand Dragons and Ten Thousand Dragons Fight As One, but other than that I'm coming up empty on social magic. Not to say that they don't have it, but it's mostly rather generic stuff, or if interesing then in a way that doesn't evoke their themes much to me, like the &quot;fight under cover of a performance&quot;-Charms.<br /> <br /> Utility-wise there's Terrestrial Ability Reinforcement which lets you share skills with others, All-Encompassing Earth Sense and Feeling the Air Technique which I always loved, there's some Air charm whose name I don't remember which lets you turn invisible... and there's Wind-Carried Words, which I've always felt should have a pretty profound effect on social life in the Realm -it's not a phone, but it's still very convenient!<br /> <br /> What effects have I missed which you think are iconic of the Dragon-Blooded? How do you see things differently? Please help me out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:45:11-08:00","id":829420,"title":"","content":"I read the title and made a list in my head.<br /> <br /> And then you listed everything I came up with already.<br /> <br /> I can tell you that Air Dragon Style is about thrown weapons (chakram usually), Earth Dragon is about being hard as a rock and unassailable, and Wood Dragon is about archery and spirits and killing someone with a touch. <br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T15:07:32-08:00","id":829427,"title":"","content":"You've hit the best ones, I feel.<br /> <br /> Myself, I've always had a soft spot for As in the Beginning (DotFA:LoC, pp. 100-101), but naturally, some reassembly might be required. The name and theme stands preserving, however: a very restricted massively powerful elemental effect, perhaps gated behind other actions than dying.<br /> <br /> From Eggs to (Element) Dragons (TCA, pp. 83-84) was also a thing I really liked, being a Charm that allowed a &quot;training camp&quot; style of education. It had basic, intermediate and advanced levels, it circulated subjects based on the seasons and it was based in War rather than Lore, brilliantly capturing the Terrestrial aesthetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T15:09:38-08:00","id":829429,"title":"","content":"How can y'all ignore Sweeten-the-Tap Method like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T15:26:38-08:00","id":829437,"title":"","content":"Wind-Carried Words and Dragon Vortex are pretty iconic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T20:48:29-08:00","id":829546,"title":"","content":"Mostly what people have already said.<br /> <br /> In practice, I've found Revelation of Associate's Hunch to be one of the most used Dragonblood charms, but it probably shouldn't be!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:17:12-08:00","id":830975,"title":"","content":"I know we already hit this one, but every single Dragon-Blooded can and should learn Wind-Carried Words. So phenomenally important.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, there are two areas that stand out for me that folks haven't already mentioned.<br /> <br /> The first are the teamwork charms, like letting more of your friends pile on one person, or doing stealth for a whole group. Dragon-Blooded were always billed as being good at teamwork (when they could stop stabbing each other in the back), and I wish we had seen more of these.<br /> <br /> The second are the Investigate charms that let you find out who someone knows and where they live just by talking to them. That's incredibly powerful, and it helps to explain why the Wyld Hunt is so effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:26:41-08:00","id":830981,"title":"","content":"Out of all the Exalted Splat Charms an Eclipse could take in Ex2, I think the only one I will truly miss is Wind-Carried Words. Yes, there were other charms that were more powerful, but that Dragonblooded charm is so freaking useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:08:33-08:00","id":830997,"title":"","content":"Since I like lists, I compile all the charms talked about in this thread and linked them to the Wiki Dump. Did I miss any?<br /> <br /> <b>Dragonblooded Charms</b><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Elemental_Bolt_Attack\" target=\"_blank\">Elemental Bolt Attack</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Dragon-Graced_Weapon\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon-Graced Weapon</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Unassailable_Body_of_(Element)_Defense\" target=\"_blank\">Unassailable Body of (Element) Defense</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Oath_of_the_Ten-Thousand_Dragons\" target=\"_blank\">Oath of the Ten Thousand Dragons</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Ten-Thousand_Dragons_Fight_as_One\" target=\"_blank\">Ten Thousand Dragons Fight As One</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Terrestrial_(Ability)_Reinforcement\" target=\"_blank\">Terrestrial Ability Reinforcement</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:All-Encompassing_Earth_Sense\" target=\"_blank\">All-Encompassing Earth Sense</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Feeling-the-Air_Technique\" target=\"_blank\">Feeling the Air Technique</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Wind-Carried_Words_Technique\" target=\"_blank\">Wind-Carried Words</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Sweeten-the-Tap_Method\" target=\"_blank\">Sweeten-the-Tap Method</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Dragon_Vortex_Attack\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Vortex Attack</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Revelation_of_Associates_Hunch\" target=\"_blank\">Revelation of Associate's Hunch</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:As_in_the_Beginning\" target=\"_blank\">As in the Beginning</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:From_Eggs_to_(Element)_Dragons\" target=\"_blank\">From Eggs to (Element) Dragons</a><br /> <br /> <b>Immaculate Martial Arts</b><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Air_Dragon_Style\" target=\"_blank\">Air Dragon Style</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Earth_Dragon_Style\" target=\"_blank\">Earth Dragon Style</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Fire_Dragon_Style\" target=\"_blank\">Fire Dragon Style</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Water_Dragon_Style\" target=\"_blank\">Water Dragon Style</a><br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Wood_Dragon_Style\" target=\"_blank\">Wood Dragon Style</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Five-Dragon_Style\" target=\"_blank\">Five Dragon Style?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-16-2016, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T09:57:08-08:00","id":831103,"title":"","content":"Enfolded in Dragons Wings is iconic to me.<br /> <br /> There is the battlefield version of a Melee-based Dragon-Blooded leading her shocktroops to break the enemy line swirling in her cutting winds that never touch her allies, of course.<br /> <br /> But there are also the not-so-secret society where a Threshold Dragon-Blooded leads a cult to venerate her by 'bleeding the unbelievers' in her Anima of throns while those 'true to the faith' are touched only by the swirling flower petals. <br /> <br /> Even the bureaucrat who uses their Anima as dramatic negotiating leverage. As rocks break every scroll in the room the Dragon-Blooded negotiating with a mortal says &quot;You are safe only because I will you to be safe. Cross me and you'll disintegrate like these ledgers you hold so dear.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:27:01-08:00","id":831251,"title":"","content":"Did anyone create a fan update for Dragonblooded? I know the book is coming out &quot;soon&quot;, but I wouldn't mind a few more non-combat charms to flesh out some Dragonblooded NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:46:12-08:00","id":831363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/829416-what-are-the-iconic-dragon-blooded-charms?p=831251#post831251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone create a fan update for Dragonblooded? I know the book is coming out &amp;quot;soon&amp;quot;, but I wouldn't mind a few more non-combat charms to flesh out some Dragonblooded NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone tried but I think I scared them off <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:08:27-08:00","id":831643,"title":"","content":"Tricky to think of many as iconic, like &quot;This is what Dragonblooded are all about&quot; or &quot;Without this, they're not Dragonblooded&quot;. <br /> <br /> Talking about general themes, just taking the Air Charms for example the themes of the Charm trees in 1e Dragonblooded book were:<br /> <br /> Linguistics - Words carried through air: Universal communication, meaning twisting and amplification, distant speech and hearing, all so long as the communication is speech through air, and then With One Mind, which is enhanced non-verbal communication and wordless coordination, through infused Air essence.<br /> <br /> Lore - Meditation and willpower to master and draw of elemental energy (kind of strange but where else do you put meditation and will, I guess?). Only Elemental Concentration helps the character learn; other Charms allow drawing on elemental energy, or channeling it.<br /> <br /> Occult - Kind of a mish mash. Spirit Mirror allows Dragonblooded to see dematerialized spirits in mirrors, Harmonious Wind-Luring Song summoning and controlling wind spirits via song, then utility spirit stopping and attacking.<br /> <br /> Stealth - Using control of air to detect surroundings without light (Feeling The Air Technique), to make no sound, to use air to call and create minor distractions, and to summon breezes to obscure traces of movement (eliminating &quot;Whose footprints are these?&quot;), Wind-Walking Technique is literal walking on air and so being able to cross flimsy beams, mud, etc with no trace, Dragon Shroud Technique is &quot;Bird of Prey&quot; / Predator style blur invisibility through command of air essence.<br /> <br /> Thrown - is mostly what you'd think. Plus using air control to turn aside weapons and make an weapons and armor from roiling winds.<br /> (I kind of think Air ended up getting the best stuff that was truly elemental in feel, maybe in part because of how omnipresent and subtle Air can be. It was kind of a contrast to me how Air Linguistics or Stealth just feels like the Dragonblooded is commanding Air, while for contrast Wood Medicine didn't really even involve plants or wood at all, which seems like a missed opportunity, when you consider how much Medicine could draw on that. Likewise not much in Ride about using plant covered terrain, or nourishing your mount on elemental plant essence, etc.).<br /> <br /> For Charms in the Dragonblooded set that are strong and useful, regardless of whether they're that in theme, I thought Testing the Waters (Water Bureaucracy) was pretty good - the Exalt just knows how a vote would fall, if a matter were put to a vote, for groups of seven or more. But it's not exactly something you can only imagine Dragonblooded knowing. Dragonblooded Investigation is all pretty useful really, although it all does ride on &quot;How difficult would a roll for this be, anyway?&quot; (in which case why buy the Charm?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}